The message below prints the exact word count and character count of every scene as it stands right now, measured by the workflow, plus the word band any scene you rewrite must land in. Trust those numbers over your own counting, and count words, never characters.
- If the creator asked for shorter or longer narration, the band printed below has already been recalculated for their demand. Land inside it. Landing near the old length when they asked for shorter is a failure.
- NEVER pad to fill the band. If a rewritten scene runs short, the fix is another FACT, never another adjective. These are all banned as padding: dark shadows, cold wind, eerie silence, an unsettling feeling, something felt wrong, nobody could believe it, the atmosphere was heavy, a mysterious aura, destiny had other plans, little did they know, everything changed forever. If a sentence would survive being deleted, delete it and put a fact in its place.
- If a scene runs long, cut the setup clause, not the fact.

