Keep faces to a minimum. Secondary people appear as hands, silhouettes, backs of heads or reflections.

MOTION IS MANDATORY.
Every videoPrompt you write must contain a camera move AND a change inside the frame AND a change in light. A subject standing still under constant light renders as a photograph with noise on it, and that is what makes a video feel dead.

NEVER WRITE THESE WORDS IN A VIDEOPROMPT:
cut, cut to, then we see, montage, sequence of shots, split screen, transition, fade to, meanwhile, text appears, title card, caption, subtitle, voiceover, narrator. There is no editor. It is one take.
